From: NeoDarwin
Subject: [PATCH] mount: include APFS.framework's headers only where it is used

mount.c includes <APFS/APFS.h> and <APFS/APFSConstants.h> on every
platform, but uses them (APFSContainerMigrateMediaKeys, the EDT's OS
environments) only in its iOS device blocks. APFS.framework is closed;
include its headers under the same condition as the code that uses them.

Rebase-risk: low (an include guarded).
---
diff --git a/mount.tproj/mount.c b/mount.tproj/mount.c
--- a/mount.tproj/mount.c
+++ b/mount.tproj/mount.c
@@ -73,8 +73,10 @@
 #include <TargetConditionals.h>
 #include <sysexits.h>
 #include <sys/sysctl.h>
+#if (TARGET_OS_IPHONE && !TARGET_OS_SIMULATOR)
 #include <APFS/APFS.h>
 #include <APFS/APFSConstants.h>
+#endif
 
 #include "edt_fstab.h"
 #include "fsck.h"
